Description: systemd-native Drcom authentication daemon for JLU
 A lightweight Drcom authentication daemon designed for the Jilin
 University campus network.  Written in C17 with first-class sd_event,
 sd_journal, and sd_daemon integration, and tuned for arm64 (with amd64
 as a fully supported secondary target).
 .
 Key features:
  * Type=notify systemd service with watchdog, hardened unit files
  * Runtime CPU feature detection (getauxval/AT_HWCAP) for portable
    arm64 binaries with NEON fast paths
  * rtnetlink link-state monitoring: reacts to interface up/down in ~1ms
  * No heavyweight dependencies beyond libsystemd
  * INI-style configuration with password-file support
